{"type":"text","timestamp":1791634528758,"sessionID":"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam","part":{"id":"prt_125bd5632001eXeHLgMcSOhCdK","messageID":"msg_125bd43a70016z5qU02YeN1xF6","sessionID":"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam","type":"text","text":"Audit complete. Findings:\n\n- `secrets-hygiene` — **keep**: only role-specific coverage (`agents/security.md` checklist, `agents/architect.md` mention), no always-on rule.\n- `no-debug-leftovers` — **keep**: near-verbatim exists in `agents/quality.md:92`, but that's an on-demand review agent; the policy makes it always-on for every session (added scope).\n- `smallest-change` — **drop**: `prompts/meta.md` (the system-wide layer, already in every session) states \"Prefer small, focused… changes… never silently expand a task\" and \"Don't do things you're not asked to do\". No way to broaden it → restates a core prompt with no added scope (criterion 3).\n- `ask-before-adding-dependencies` — **keep**: only in `agents/developer.md` (developer-only); policy adds session-wide scope.\n- `keep-it-committed` — **keep**: only in `agents/developer.md` (developer-only); policy adds session-wide scope.\n\nRemoving `smallest-change.md` per TASK-6.","time":{"start":1791634527794,"end":1791634528756}}}
