{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791634560246,"sessionID":"ses_eda42451effe3iTssKr1TVXCGU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01_Dhyg0qEFLZaW5QmXaR5P9336","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Tasks: policies\n2: \n3: id: medical\n4: analyst: analyst\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n8: \n9: ## Overview\n10: \n11: Add a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\n12: small set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\n13: plain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\n14: the four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\n15: real spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n16: \n17: Scope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n18: - Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n19:   `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n20: - Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n21:   brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n22:   those, but the brief is explicit).\n23: - Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n24:   two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n25: \n26: Notes for @developer (not blockers):\n27: - The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n28:   against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n29: - The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n30:   proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n31:   `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n32:   (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n33:   session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n34:   developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n35:   be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n36:   `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n37: - The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n38:   `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n39:   TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n40: \n41: ## Task breakdown\n42: \n43: ### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n44: \n45: - **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n46:   logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n47:   (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n48:   always/never rule per the brief's format.\n49: - **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n50: - **Depends**: none\n51: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n52:   affected.\n53: \n54: ### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n55: \n56: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n57:   output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n58:   issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n59: - **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n60: - **Depends**: none\n61: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n62: \n63: ### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n64: \n65: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n66:   that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n67:   expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n68:   instruction.\n69: - **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n70: - **Depends**: none\n71: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n72:   avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n73: \n74: ### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n75: \n76: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n77:   before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n78: - **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n79: - **Depends**: none\n80: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n81:   prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n82: \n83: ### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n84: \n85: - **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n86:   work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n87: - **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n88: - **Depends**: none\n89: - **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n90: \n91: ### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n92: \n93: - **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n94:   decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n95:   (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n96:   entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n97:   skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n98:   record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n99: - **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n100:   removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n101: - **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n102: - **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n103:   the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n104:   brief's criteria.\n105: \n106: ## Notes / open questions\n107: \n108: - The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n109:   suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n110:   TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n111:   drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n112:   scope, not a scope expansion.\n113: - No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.\n\n(End of file - total 113 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Tasks: policies\n\nid: medical\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\nsmall set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\nplain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\nthe four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\nreal spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md","text":"# Tasks: policies\n\nid: medical\nanalyst: analyst\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n\n## Overview\n\nAdd a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\nsmall set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\nplain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\nthe four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\nreal spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n\nScope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n  brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n  those, but the brief is explicit).\n- Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n  two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n\nNotes for @developer (not blockers):\n- The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n  against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n- The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n  proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n  `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n  (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n  session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n  developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n  be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n  `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n- The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n  `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n  TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n\n## Task breakdown\n\n### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n  logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n  (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n  always/never rule per the brief's format.\n- **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n  affected.\n\n### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n  output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n  issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n- **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n\n### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n  that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n  expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n  instruction.\n- **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n  avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n\n### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n  before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n- **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n  prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n\n### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n\n- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n  work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n- **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n- **Depends**: none\n- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n\n### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n\n- **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n  decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n  (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n  entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n  skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n  record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n- **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n  removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n- **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n- **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n  the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n  brief's criteria.\n\n## Notes / open questions\n\n- The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n  suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n  TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n  drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n  scope, not a scope expansion.\n- No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":113,"totalLines":113,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md","time":{"start":1791634560059,"end":1791634560240}},"id":"prt_125bdd3f4001uNozsDdBvMwKly","sessionID":"ses_eda42451effe3iTssKr1TVXCGU","messageID":"msg_125bdce88001D707AnsRp6kthc"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791634560336,"sessionID":"ses_eda42451effe3iTssKr1TVXCGU","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_02_mtz8Mx1vsNyKY3VNNsvj3122","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Implementation: policies\n2: \n3: id: medical\n4: developer: developer\n5: date: 2026-10-10\n6: \n7: <!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n8: \n9: ## Summary\n10: \n11: Added a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog with a\n12: small set of global, always-on policy files, following the brief's format\n13: (plain markdown, one rule per file, filename is the identity, no frontmatter,\n14: short: one-line heading + rule + at most a line or two of why). Four of the\n15: five proposed starter policies shipped; the fifth (`smallest-change`) was\n16: dropped by the TASK-6 audit because it merely restated an existing\n17: system-wide instruction. No code, build, or test tooling exists in this repo,\n18: so verification was content review against the brief's decision criteria.\n19: \n20: Final set (sorted as the catalog concatenates them):\n21: \n22: - `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n23: - `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n24: - `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n25: - `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n26: \n27: ## Changes\n28: \n29: TASK-1: Created `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` — never commit, log, print or\n30: hardcode secrets/tokens/keys/credentials; read them from env/untracked config.\n31: Universal, always-on, no overlap with an always-on rule in this catalog.\n32: \n33: TASK-2: Created `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` — leave no debug output,\n34: commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a tracked issue behind.\n35: \n36: TASK-3: Created `policies/smallest-change.md` — smallest change that satisfies\n37: the task; no refactoring/tidying of adjacent code, no scope expansion.\n38: \n39: TASK-4: Created `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` — do not add a\n40: dependency without explicit approval; a dependency is a lasting project cost.\n41: \n42: TASK-5: Created `policies/keep-it-committed.md` — leave no uncommitted work\n43: behind; record changes before finishing.\n44: \n45: TASK-6: Audited all five files against the brief's four decision criteria and\n46: the catalog content that actually exists in this repo (`prompts/*.md`,\n47: `agents/*.md`, `skills/`). Outcome: **dropped `policies/smallest-change.md`**;\n48: kept the other four. Rationale per file:\n49: \n50: - `secrets-hygiene` — KEEP. Existing coverage is role-specific and on-demand:\n51:   `agents/security.md` lists hardcoded credentials/tokens as a review\n52:   checklist, and `agents/architect.md` mentions secrets management as one\n53:   operational concern. No always-on rule existed; a global policy is a real\n54:   behavioural change. Universal, short, always/never. Passes.\n55: - `no-debug-leftovers` — KEEP. `agents/quality.md:92` carries near-identical\n56:   wording (\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO\n57:   comments left without a tracking issue\"), but that is an on-demand,\n58:   read-only code-quality *review* agent. Promoting it to an always-on rule\n59:   that every session sees is added scope, not a restatement. Passes.\n60: - `smallest-change` — DROP. `prompts/meta.md` is the system-wide layer that\n61:   already reaches every session: \"Prefer small, focused, well-understood\n62:   changes over broad sweeping ones. When scope is unclear, ask rather than\n63:   guess — never silently expand a task.\" and \"Don't do things you're not asked\n64:   to do.\" It is also repeated in `agents/developer.md`, `agents/devops.md` and\n65:   `agents/sysadmin.md`. There is no way to make this meaningfully broader than\n66:   an instruction that is *already* global, so per criterion 3 (restates a core\n67:   instruction with no added scope) it was removed. The file was created under\n68:   TASK-3 and deleted here, as the brief and tasks explicitly anticipated (\"the\n69:   final set may be fewer than five\").\n70: - `ask-before-adding-dependencies` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md:51`\n71:   (\"Do not install packages without asking first\") covers it, and that is\n72:   developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` says nothing about dependencies. The\n73:   policy makes the constraint hold for every session, which is added scope.\n74:   Passes.\n75: - `keep-it-committed` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md` has the commit /\n76:   clean-worktree steps, developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` does not cover\n77:   committing. As a universal always-on rule it adds scope. Passes.\n78: \n79: All four kept files pass the four criteria: universal (every project, language\n80: and task), a short always/never constraint (≤ 3 lines of body), no pure\n81: restatement of an always-on skill or prompt, and not situational. No\n82: frontmatter, no id, no README/hidden files/symlinks in `policies/`.\n83: \n84: ## Known issues / follow-ups\n85: \n86: - The dedupe check in TASK-6 was necessarily limited to the content present in\n87:   this repository. The brief references manigot's `internal/session/policies.go`,\n88:   its `AGENTS.md`, and \"~70 more\" skills (`go-code-review`,\n89:   `typescript-guidelines`, `security-best-practices`, `test-driven-development`,\n90:   …) that do not exist in this checkout. Those referenced skills may later\n91:   partly overlap with `secrets-hygiene` or `no-debug-leftovers`; if so, this\n92:   set should be re-checked against them.\n93: - `keep-it-committed` is phrased to apply session-wide, but read-only agents\n94:   (`reviewer`, `quality`, `security`, `tldr`) have nothing to commit; the rule\n95:   is a hygiene constraint on final repo state, not an instruction that every\n96:   agent must run `git commit`.\n\n(End of file - total 96 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation: policies\n\nid: medical\ndeveloper: developer\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog with a\nsmall set of global, always-on policy files, following the brief's format\n(plain markdown, one rule per file, filename is the identity, no frontmatter,\nshort: one-line heading + rule + at most a line or two of why). Four of the\nfive proposed starter policies shipped; the fifth (`smallest-change`) was\ndropped by the TASK-6 audit because it merely restated an existing\nsystem-wide instruction. No code, build, or test tooling exists in this repo,\nso verification was content review against the brief's decision criteria.\n\nFinal set (sorted as the catalog concatenates them):","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md","text":"# Implementation: policies\n\nid: medical\ndeveloper: developer\ndate: 2026-10-10\n\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog with a\nsmall set of global, always-on policy files, following the brief's format\n(plain markdown, one rule per file, filename is the identity, no frontmatter,\nshort: one-line heading + rule + at most a line or two of why). Four of the\nfive proposed starter policies shipped; the fifth (`smallest-change`) was\ndropped by the TASK-6 audit because it merely restated an existing\nsystem-wide instruction. No code, build, or test tooling exists in this repo,\nso verification was content review against the brief's decision criteria.\n\nFinal set (sorted as the catalog concatenates them):\n\n- `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n- `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n- `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n- `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n\n## Changes\n\nTASK-1: Created `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` — never commit, log, print or\nhardcode secrets/tokens/keys/credentials; read them from env/untracked config.\nUniversal, always-on, no overlap with an always-on rule in this catalog.\n\nTASK-2: Created `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` — leave no debug output,\ncommented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a tracked issue behind.\n\nTASK-3: Created `policies/smallest-change.md` — smallest change that satisfies\nthe task; no refactoring/tidying of adjacent code, no scope expansion.\n\nTASK-4: Created `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` — do not add a\ndependency without explicit approval; a dependency is a lasting project cost.\n\nTASK-5: Created `policies/keep-it-committed.md` — leave no uncommitted work\nbehind; record changes before finishing.\n\nTASK-6: Audited all five files against the brief's four decision criteria and\nthe catalog content that actually exists in this repo (`prompts/*.md`,\n`agents/*.md`, `skills/`). Outcome: **dropped `policies/smallest-change.md`**;\nkept the other four. Rationale per file:\n\n- `secrets-hygiene` — KEEP. Existing coverage is role-specific and on-demand:\n  `agents/security.md` lists hardcoded credentials/tokens as a review\n  checklist, and `agents/architect.md` mentions secrets management as one\n  operational concern. No always-on rule existed; a global policy is a real\n  behavioural change. Universal, short, always/never. Passes.\n- `no-debug-leftovers` — KEEP. `agents/quality.md:92` carries near-identical\n  wording (\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO\n  comments left without a tracking issue\"), but that is an on-demand,\n  read-only code-quality *review* agent. Promoting it to an always-on rule\n  that every session sees is added scope, not a restatement. Passes.\n- `smallest-change` — DROP. `prompts/meta.md` is the system-wide layer that\n  already reaches every session: \"Prefer small, focused, well-understood\n  changes over broad sweeping ones. When scope is unclear, ask rather than\n  guess — never silently expand a task.\" and \"Don't do things you're not asked\n  to do.\" It is also repeated in `agents/developer.md`, `agents/devops.md` and\n  `agents/sysadmin.md`. There is no way to make this meaningfully broader than\n  an instruction that is *already* global, so per criterion 3 (restates a core\n  instruction with no added scope) it was removed. The file was created under\n  TASK-3 and deleted here, as the brief and tasks explicitly anticipated (\"the\n  final set may be fewer than five\").\n- `ask-before-adding-dependencies` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md:51`\n  (\"Do not install packages without asking first\") covers it, and that is\n  developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` says nothing about dependencies. The\n  policy makes the constraint hold for every session, which is added scope.\n  Passes.\n- `keep-it-committed` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md` has the commit /\n  clean-worktree steps, developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` does not cover\n  committing. As a universal always-on rule it adds scope. Passes.\n\nAll four kept files pass the four criteria: universal (every project, language\nand task), a short always/never constraint (≤ 3 lines of body), no pure\nrestatement of an always-on skill or prompt, and not situational. No\nfrontmatter, no id, no README/hidden files/symlinks in `policies/`.\n\n## Known issues / follow-ups\n\n- The dedupe check in TASK-6 was necessarily limited to the content present in\n  this repository. The brief references manigot's `internal/session/policies.go`,\n  its `AGENTS.md`, and \"~70 more\" skills (`go-code-review`,\n  `typescript-guidelines`, `security-best-practices`, `test-driven-development`,\n  …) that do not exist in this checkout. Those referenced skills may later\n  partly overlap with `secrets-hygiene` or `no-debug-leftovers`; if so, this\n  set should be re-checked against them.\n- `keep-it-committed` is phrased to apply session-wide, but read-only agents\n  (`reviewer`, `quality`, `security`, `tldr`) have nothing to commit; the rule\n  is a hygiene constraint on final repo state, not an instruction that every\n  agent must run `git commit`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":96,"totalLines":96,"truncated":false}},"title":"docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md","time":{"start":1791634560175,"end":1791634560321}},"id":"prt_125bdd451001Ye0xGODVxppWdI","sessionID":"ses_eda42451effe3iTssKr1TVXCGU","messageID":"msg_125bdce88001D707AnsRp6kthc"}}
