ore you sprawl\\n10: \\n11: - Don't chain a large batch of actions unattended just because you technically\\n12:   can. When a request is ambiguous, or the next step is broad, irreversible,\\n13:   or a guess about intent, check in rather than running with your best guess.\\n14:   A human is right here — use that.\\n15: - This does not mean stall on everything. Small, obvious, reversible steps\\n16:   don't need a check-in. Save it for the moments where a wrong guess would\\n17:   cost real rework.\\n18: \\n19: ## Talk, don't just deliver a form\\n20: \\n21: - If your agent instructions describe a structured deliverable — a verdict, a\\n22:   fixed set of sections, a scored rubric — that shape is for when you're\\n23:   actually asked to review or decide something, or when you're wrapping one\\n24:   up. It is not the required shape of every reply.\\n25: - When the human is thinking out loud, exploring an idea, or just asking\\n26:   questions, have a normal conversation. Don't force the conversation toward\\n27:   a formal output it doesn't need yet.\\n\\n(End of file - total 27 lines)\\n</content>\",\"metadata\":{\"preview\":\"# manigot — interactive-session addendum\\n\\nThis layers under the system-wide meta prompt and only reaches interactive\\nsessions — a human is directly present and able to answer questions, unlike\\n`--print`/`mg jdi` runs, which never see this file. Your agent file and the\\nproject context remain the operative per-role instructions; this addendum\\nadjusts how you carry them out when someone is actually here to talk to.\\n\\n## Ask before you sprawl\\n\\n- Don't chain a large batch of actions unattended just because you technically\\n  can. When a request is ambiguous, or the next step is broad, irreversible,\\n  or a guess about intent, check in rather than running with your best guess.\\n  A human is right here — use that.\\n- This does not mean stall on everything. Small, obvious, reversible steps\\n  don't need a check-in. Save it for the moments where a wrong guess would\\n  cost real rework.\\n\\n## Talk, don't just deliver a form\\n\",\"truncated\":false,\"loaded\":[],\"display\":{\"type\":\"file\",\"path\":\"/workspace/prompts/interactive.md\",\"text\":\"# manigot — interactive-session addendum\\n\\nThis layers under the system-wide meta prompt and only reaches interactive\\nsessions — a human is directly present and able to answer questions, unlike\\n`--print`/`mg jdi` runs, which never see this file. Your agent file and the\\nproject context remain the operative per-role instructions; this addendum\\nadjusts how you carry them out when someone is actually here to talk to.\\n\\n## Ask before you sprawl\\n\\n- Don't chain a large batch of actions unattended just because you technically\\n  can. When a request is ambiguous, or the next step is broad, irreversible,\\n  or a guess about intent, check in rather than running with your best guess.\\n  A human is right here — use that.\\n- This does not mean stall on everything. Small, obvious, reversible steps\\n  don't need a check-in. Save it for the moments where a wrong guess would\\n  cost real rework.\\n\\n## Talk, don't just deliver a form\\n\\n- If your agent instructions describe a structured deliverable — a verdict, a\\n  fixed set of sections, a scored rubric — that shape is for when you're\\n  actually asked to review or decide something, or when you're wrapping one\\n  up. It is not the required shape of every reply.\\n- When the human is thinking out loud, exploring an idea, or just asking\\n  questions, have a normal conversation. Don't force the conversation toward\\n  a formal output it doesn't need yet.\",\"lineStart\":1,\"lineEnd\":27,\"totalLines\":27,\"truncated\":false}},\"title\":\"prompts/interactive.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634522672,\"end\":1791634522856}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd419e001IHkQWX4T0vDcjy\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd2e6f001KuCrytHQOJ5UUO\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791634522900,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_01_G8mWkUNTGM7HzRG4iBZe1728\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /workspace && sed -n '80,100p' agents/quality.md && echo \\\"=== developer 45-90 ===\\\" && sed -n '45,90p' agents/developer.md\"},\"output\":\"- Are new functions/classes/components a reasonable size, or are they doing too much?\\n- Is responsibility clearly assigned — does each unit have a clear owner?\\n\\n**Consistency**\\n- Does the new code follow the same patterns as the existing codebase?\\n- Same error handling style, same naming conventions, same file organisation?\\n- If the codebase uses a specific pattern everywhere, new code should follow it — not introduce a different one without reason.\\n- Inconsistency is a maintenance burden: future readers have to understand two ways of doing the same thing.\\n\\n**Modern practices for this stack**\\n- PHP: proper typing, return types, no raw queries, no `var_dump` left in, appropriate Laravel conventions (form requests, policies, resources), no static methods where dependency injection fits better\\n- JS/Svelte: no `var`, appropriate reactivity patterns, no direct DOM manipulation where Svelte handles it, props typed where possible\\n- General: no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO comments left without a tracking issue\\n\\n**Defensiveness**\\n- Are inputs validated where they enter the system?\\n- Are error states handled explicitly or silently swallowed?\\n- Are edge cases considered — empty arrays, null values, zero, large inputs, concurrent access?\\n\\n## What you do NOT do\\n\\n=== developer 45-90 ===\\n\\n**Step 1 — Read** the relevant files before touching anything.\\n\\n**Step 2 — Implement** exactly what the task requires. Nothing more.\\n- Make the smallest change that correctly fulfills the task\\n- Do not refactor adjacent code unless the task explicitly requires it\\n- Do not install packages without asking first\\n- If the task turns out to be more complex than described: stop and report back, do not expand scope\\n\\n**Step 3 — Commit** once the task is complete. One commit per task is the\\nrecommended pattern, but the exact message format is not required — the whole\\nbranch is squashed into a single commit at `mg done`, so per-task commit\\nhygiene is not a review criterion.\\n```\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -m \\\"short description\\\"\\n```\\n\\nA task should be committed before moving to the next one. When you finish,\\nleave the worktree clean: nothing uncommitted, including files earlier agents\\nleft behind (e.g. the analyst's `tasks.md`).\\n\\n**Step 4 — Repeat** for the next task.\\n\\n## After all tasks are done\\n\\nWrite a summary to `implementation.md` in the job directory:\\n\\n```markdown\\n## Summary\\n\\nBrief overall description of what was implemented.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1: what was done, which files were changed and why\\nTASK-2: ...\\n\\n## Known issues / follow-ups\\n\\nAnything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope.\\nIf nothing: write \\\"none\\\".\\n```\\n\\nThen commit `implementation.md`:\\n```\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"- Are new functions/classes/components a reasonable size, or are they doing too much?\\n- Is responsibility clearly assigned — does each unit have a clear owner?\\n\\n**Consistency**\\n- Does the new code follow the same patterns as the existing codebase?\\n- Same error handling style, same naming conventions, same file organisation?\\n- If the codebase uses a specific pattern everywhere, new code should follow it — not introduce a different one without reason.\\n- Inconsistency is a maintenance burden: future readers have to understand two ways of doing the same thing.\\n\\n**Modern practices for this stack**\\n- PHP: proper typing, return types, no raw queries, no `var_dump` left in, appropriate Laravel conventions (form requests, policies, resources), no static methods where dependency injection fits better\\n- JS/Svelte: no `var`, appropriate reactivity patterns, no direct DOM manipulation where Svelte handles it, props typed where possible\\n- General: no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO comments left without a tracking issue\\n\\n**Defensiveness**\\n- Are inputs validated where they enter the system?\\n- Are error states handled explicitly or silently swallowed?\\n- Are edge cases considered — empty arrays, null values, zero, large inputs, concurrent access?\\n\\n## What you do NOT do\\n\\n=== developer 45-90 ===\\n\\n**Step 1 — Read** the relevant files before touching anything.\\n\\n**Step 2 — Implement** exactly what the task requires. Nothing more.\\n- Make the smallest change that correctly fulfills the task\\n- Do not refactor adjacent code unless the task explicitly requires it\\n- Do not install packages without asking first\\n- If the task turns out to be more complex than described: stop and report back, do not expand scope\\n\\n**Step 3 — Commit** once the task is complete. One commit per task is the\\nrecommended pattern, but the exact message format is not required — the whole\\nbranch is squashed into a single commit at `mg done`, so per-task commit\\nhygiene is not a review criterion.\\n```\\ngit add -A\\ngit commit -m \\\"short description\\\"\\n```\\n\\nA task should be committed before moving to the next one. When you finish,\\nleave the worktree clean: nothing uncommitted, including files earlier agents\\nleft behind (e.g. the analyst's `tasks.md`).\\n\\n**Step 4 — Repeat** for the next task.\\n\\n## After all tasks are done\\n\\nWrite a summary to `implementation.md` in the job directory:\\n\\n```markdown\\n## Summary\\n\\nBrief overall description of what was implemented.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1: what was done, which files were changed and why\\nTASK-2: ...\\n\\n## Known issues / follow-ups\\n\\nAnything that came up during implementation that wasn't in scope.\\nIf nothing: write \\\"none\\\".\\n```\\n\\nThen commit `implementation.md`:\\n```\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"cd /workspace && sed -n '80,100p' agents/quality.md && echo \\\"=== developer 45-90 ===\\\" && sed -n '45,90p' agents/developer.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634522768,\"end\":1791634522867}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd42380012rUFky35inGRhG\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd2e6f001KuCrytHQOJ5UUO\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634523061,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd4385001dLPZ3Lm6p7WH46\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd2e6f001KuCrytHQOJ5UUO\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":36565,\"input\":4493,\"output\":115,\"reasoning\":597,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":31360}},\"cost\":0.00119523}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634524361,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd48c5001RbrwvVU8rvBp39\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd43a70016z5qU02YeN1xF6\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791634528758,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd5632001eXeHLgMcSOhCdK\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd43a70016z5qU02YeN1xF6\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Audit complete. Findings:\\n\\n- `secrets-hygiene` — **keep**: only role-specific coverage (`agents/security.md` checklist, `agents/architect.md` mention), no always-on rule.\\n- `no-debug-leftovers` — **keep**: near-verbatim exists in `agents/quality.md:92`, but that's an on-demand review agent; the policy makes it always-on for every session (added scope).\\n- `smallest-change` — **drop**: `prompts/meta.md` (the system-wide layer, already in every session) states \\\"Prefer small, focused… changes… never silently expand a task\\\" and \\\"Don't do things you're not asked to do\\\". No way to broaden it → restates a core prompt with no added scope (criterion 3).\\n- `ask-before-adding-dependencies` — **keep**: only in `agents/developer.md` (developer-only); policy adds session-wide scope.\\n- `keep-it-committed` — **keep**: only in `agents/developer.md` (developer-only); policy adds session-wide scope.\\n\\nRemoving `smallest-change.md` per TASK-6.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634527794,\"end\":1791634528756}}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791634528782,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_00_zQTggQM5t5tyVveXwBc56107\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /workspace && rm policies/smallest-change.md && ls -la policies/ && git status --short\"},\"output\":\"total 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 claude claude 4096 Oct 10 12:15 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 9 claude claude 4096 Oct 10 12:14 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  186 Oct 10 12:15 ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  166 Oct 10 12:15 keep-it-committed.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  191 Oct 10 12:14 no-debug-leftovers.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  220 Oct 10 12:14 secrets-hygiene.md\\n M docs/jobs/medical_policies/session.log\\n D policies/smallest-change.md\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"total 24\\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 claude claude 4096 Oct 10 12:15 .\\ndrwxr-xr-x 9 claude claude 4096 Oct 10 12:14 ..\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  186 Oct 10 12:15 ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  166 Oct 10 12:15 keep-it-committed.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  191 Oct 10 12:14 no-debug-leftovers.md\\n-rw-r--r-- 1 claude claude  220 Oct 10 12:14 secrets-hygiene.md\\n M docs/jobs/medical_policies/session.log\\n D policies/smallest-change.md\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"cd /workspace && rm policies/smallest-change.md && ls -la policies/ && git status --short\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634528731,\"end\":1791634528764}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd5961001EJz5W7PfoYxbdF\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd43a70016z5qU02YeN1xF6\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634528829,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd5a30001nLvieZ37M4pCsN\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd43a70016z5qU02YeN1xF6\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":38702,\"input\":1110,\"output\":304,\"reasoning\":808,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":36480}},\"cost\":0.00094314}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634530055,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd5f05001Gt40BXO8SNVR5L\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd5a3a001XREryb9OLeRFxd\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791634531728,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"bash\",\"callID\":\"call_00_KbgtOOoq4NIg79QyMf7O5344\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd /workspace && git add -A && git commit -q -m \\\"policies: drop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\\" && git log --oneline -1\"},\"output\":\"cd9f132 policies: drop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"cd9f132 policies: drop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"cd /workspace && git add -A && git commit -q -m \\\"policies: drop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\\" && git log --oneline -1\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634531679,\"end\":1791634531723}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd64d40019REEwmbc64UE3V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd5a3a001XREryb9OLeRFxd\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634531767,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd65a8001QZM90gJoc2w5Yu\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd5a3a001XREryb9OLeRFxd\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":39277,\"input\":241,\"output\":75,\"reasoning\":305,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":38656}},\"cost\":0.000380118}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634533252,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd6b800015EDAos5V2FFeoG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791634539449,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_A7VWZbi49JJOo2ajsQzG7660\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"# Implementation: policies\\n\\nid: medical\\ndeveloper: developer\\ndate: 2026-10-10\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdded a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog with a\\nsmall set of global, always-on policy files, following the brief's format\\n(plain markdown, one rule per file, filename is the identity, no frontmatter,\\nshort: one-line heading + rule + at most a line or two of why). Four of the\\nfive proposed starter policies shipped; the fifth (`smallest-change`) was\\ndropped by the TASK-6 audit because it merely restated an existing\\nsystem-wide instruction. No code, build, or test tooling exists in this repo,\\nso verification was content review against the brief's decision criteria.\\n\\nFinal set (sorted as the catalog concatenates them):\\n\\n- `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\\n- `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\\n- `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\\n- `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1: Created `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` — never commit, log, print or\\nhardcode secrets/tokens/keys/credentials; read them from env/untracked config.\\nUniversal, always-on, no overlap with an always-on rule in this catalog.\\n\\nTASK-2: Created `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` — leave no debug output,\\ncommented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a tracked issue behind.\\n\\nTASK-3: Created `policies/smallest-change.md` — smallest change that satisfies\\nthe task; no refactoring/tidying of adjacent code, no scope expansion.\\n\\nTASK-4: Created `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` — do not add a\\ndependency without explicit approval; a dependency is a lasting project cost.\\n\\nTASK-5: Created `policies/keep-it-committed.md` — leave no uncommitted work\\nbehind; record changes before finishing.\\n\\nTASK-6: Audited all five files against the brief's four decision criteria and\\nthe catalog content that actually exists in this repo (`prompts/*.md`,\\n`agents/*.md`, `skills/`). Outcome: **dropped `policies/smallest-change.md`**;\\nkept the other four. Rationale per file:\\n\\n- `secrets-hygiene` — KEEP. Existing coverage is role-specific and on-demand:\\n  `agents/security.md` lists hardcoded credentials/tokens as a review\\n  checklist, and `agents/architect.md` mentions secrets management as one\\n  operational concern. No always-on rule existed; a global policy is a real\\n  behavioural change. Universal, short, always/never. Passes.\\n- `no-debug-leftovers` — KEEP. `agents/quality.md:92` carries near-identical\\n  wording (\\\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO\\n  comments left without a tracking issue\\\"), but that is an on-demand,\\n  read-only code-quality *review* agent. Promoting it to an always-on rule\\n  that every session sees is added scope, not a restatement. Passes.\\n- `smallest-change` — DROP. `prompts/meta.md` is the system-wide layer that\\n  already reaches every session: \\\"Prefer small, focused, well-understood\\n  changes over broad sweeping ones. When scope is unclear, ask rather than\\n  guess — never silently expand a task.\\\" and \\\"Don't do things you're not asked\\n  to do.\\\" It is also repeated in `agents/developer.md`, `agents/devops.md` and\\n  `agents/sysadmin.md`. There is no way to make this meaningfully broader than\\n  an instruction that is *already* global, so per criterion 3 (restates a core\\n  instruction with no added scope) it was removed. The file was created under\\n  TASK-3 and deleted here, as the brief and tasks explicitly anticipated (\\\"the\\n  final set may be fewer than five\\\").\\n- `ask-before-adding-dependencies` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md:51`\\n  (\\\"Do not install packages without asking first\\\") covers it, and that is\\n  developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` says nothing about dependencies. The\\n  policy makes the constraint hold for every session, which is added scope.\\n  Passes.\\n- `keep-it-committed` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md` has the commit /\\n  clean-worktree steps, developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` does not cover\\n  committing. As a universal always-on rule it adds scope. Passes.\\n\\nAll four kept files pass the four criteria: universal (every project, language\\nand task), a short always/never constraint (≤ 3 lines of body), no pure\\nrestatement of an always-on skill or prompt, and not situational. No\\nfrontmatter, no id, no README/hidden files/symlinks in `policies/`.\\n\\n## Known issues / follow-ups\\n\\n- The dedupe check in TASK-6 was necessarily limited to the content present in\\n  this repository. The brief references manigot's `internal/session/policies.go`,\\n  its `AGENTS.md`, and \\\"~70 more\\\" skills (`go-code-review`,\\n  `typescript-guidelines`, `security-best-practices`, `test-driven-development`,\\n  …) that do not exist in this checkout. Those referenced skills may later\\n  partly overlap with `secrets-hygiene` or `no-debug-leftovers`; if so, this\\n  set should be re-checked against them.\\n- `keep-it-committed` is phrased to apply session-wide, but read-only agents\\n  (`reviewer`, `quality`, `security`, `tldr`) have nothing to commit; the rule\\n  is a hygiene constraint on final repo state, not an instruction that every\\n  agent must run `git commit`.\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md\"},\"output\":\"Wrote file successfully.\",\"metadata\":{\"diagnostics\":{},\"filepath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md\",\"exists\":true,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634539420,\"end\":1791634539446}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd703d001SN3FiCg5jymgPh\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791634539501,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd7000001vAK2Iy8wepaccq\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now writing the implementation summary.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634534400,\"end\":1791634539497}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634539577,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd841b001hwAnDlvEP9Xzeg\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":40823,\"input\":138,\"output\":1377,\"reasoning\":140,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":39168}},\"cost\":0.001048404}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634541120,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd8a3e001lVhDmwcI8bMpaC\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd84250012vgwqYi85keHP8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"t