\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Write implementation.md summary and commit\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n  }\\n]\",\"metadata\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"TASK-1: author policies/secrets-hygiene.md\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"TASK-2: author policies/no-debug-leftovers.md\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"TASK-3: author policies/smallest-change.md\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"TASK-4: author policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"TASK-5: author policies/keep-it-committed.md\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"TASK-6: audit policies against brief criteria; trim/drop; record\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"},{\"content\":\"Write implementation.md summary and commit\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"priority\":\"high\"}],\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"0 todos\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634546923,\"end\":1791634546928}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd9ed8001WpnIrFBir0e4kb\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd96c3001rJ5MWKpNGvjgYT\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634547031,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bda147001Gswr7fkYY4xZKY\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd96c3001rJ5MWKpNGvjgYT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":42096,\"input\":273,\"output\":250,\"reasoning\":101,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":41472}},\"cost\":0.000375966}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634548297,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bda63c0014Bu0kNjO8voozy\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bda153001bEwNOBgXdVGQdT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791634550133,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bda71c0019Pb7ReKwxLbt78\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bda153001bEwNOBgXdVGQdT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. All tasks implemented and committed on `feature/medical_policies` (branch matches the brief), working tree clean.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdded the new top-level `policies/` catalog directory with short, universal, always-on policy files — plain markdown, no frontmatter, one rule per file.\\n\\n**Final set (4 files):**\\n- `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\\n- `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\\n- `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\\n- `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\\n\\n**TASK-6 audit outcome — dropped `smallest-change`:** every other proposed rule only existed as a role-specific or on-demand instruction (`agents/security.md`, `agents/quality.md`, `agents/developer.md`), so promoting it to a global policy added real scope. `smallest-change` did not: `prompts/meta.md`, the system-wide layer already in every session, states \\\"Prefer small, focused… changes… never silently expand a task\\\" and \\\"Don't do things you're not asked to do.\\\" Per criterion 3, a rule that rules a *already-global* instruction with no added scope was removed. The brief and tasks explicitly anticipated a final set smaller than five.\\n\\n**Commits (one per task, then the summary):** `0c6737e`, `6b6002b`, `26a6159`, `172df01`, `7e415ae`, `cd9f132`, `74d0beb`.\\n\\n**Verification:** no build/test tooling exists in this repo, so verification was content review against the brief's criteria. Confirmed no frontmatter, no README, no hidden files, and no symlinks in `policies/` (the catalog scan's exclusions).\\n\\nOne caveat recorded in `implementation.md`: the dedupe check was limited to the content present in this checkout — manigot's `internal/session/policies.go`, its `AGENTS.md`, and the \\\"~70 more\\\" skills referenced by the brief are not here, so those should be re-checked later for overlap.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634548508,\"end\":1791634550129}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634550200,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bdada2001uNioLKZIehuuF8\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bda153001bEwNOBgXdVGQdT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":42821,\"input\":384,\"output\":453,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":41984}},\"cost\":0.000455352}}\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..043e714\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+# Tasks: policies\n+\n+id: medical\n+analyst: analyst\n+date: 2026-10-10\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Add a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\n+small set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\n+plain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\n+the four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\n+real spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n+\n+Scope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n+- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n+  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n+- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n+  brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n+  those, but the brief is explicit).\n+- Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n+  two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n+\n+Notes for @developer (not blockers):\n+- The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n+  against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n+- The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n+  proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n+  `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n+  (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n+  session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n+  developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n+  be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n+  `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n+- The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n+  `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n+  TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n+\n+## Task breakdown\n+\n+### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n+  logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n+  (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n+  always/never rule per the brief's format.\n+- **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n+  affected.\n+\n+### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n+  output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n+  issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n+- **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n+\n+### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n+  that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n+  expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n+  instruction.\n+- **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n+  avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n+\n+### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n+  before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n+- **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n+  prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n+\n+### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n+  work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n+- **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n+\n+### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n+\n+- **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n+  decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n+  (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n+  entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n+  skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n+  record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n+- **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n+  removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n+- **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n+- **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n+  the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n+  brief's criteria.\n+\n+## Notes / open questions\n+\n+- The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n+  suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n+  TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n+  drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n+  scope, not a scope expansion.\n+- No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tokens.json b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tokens.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..bbbf151\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tokens.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"agent\": \"analyst\",\n+    \"attempt\": 1,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-10T12:14:07.370971307Z\",\n+    \"inputTokens\": 27503,\n+    \"outputTokens\": 3045,\n+    \"cacheReadTokens\": 198144,\n+    \"reasoningTokens\": 2733,\n+    \"costUSD\": 0.008186682\n+  }\n+]\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/medical_policies/verdict.md b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/verdict.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7c92dd5\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/verdict.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+# Verdict: policies\n+\n+id: medical\n+reviewer:\n+date:\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n+\n+## Review\n+\n+<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n+     notes: ...\n+\n+TASK-2: ...\n+-->\n+\n+## Security\n+\n+<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n+\n+## Overall\n+\n+<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n+<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\ndiff --git a/policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md b/policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..113f3be\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Ask before adding dependencies\n+\n+Do not add a dependency without explicit approval.\n+A new dependency is a lasting cost to the whole project, so surface the need\n+and let a human decide.\ndiff --git a/policies/keep-it-committed.md b/policies/keep-it-committed.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3cdb48e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/keep-it-committed.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Keep it committed\n+\n+Leave no uncommitted work behind.\n+Record changes in the project before finishing so nothing is lost or left in\n+an ambiguous half-finished state.\ndiff --git a/policies/no-debug-leftovers.md b/policies/no-debug-leftovers.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f992a84\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/no-debug-leftovers.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# No debug leftovers\n+\n+Leave no debug output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a\n+tracked issue behind.\n+Remove them before finishing so the change ships only what it needs.\ndiff --git a/policies/secrets-hygiene.md b/policies/secrets-hygiene.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7cd6749\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/secrets-hygiene.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Secrets hygiene\n+\n+Never commit, log, print, or hardcode secrets, tokens, keys, or credentials.\n+Read them from the environment or untracked config, and keep them out of\n+source, diffs, command output, and error messages.\n","metadata":{"output":"...\n\nrop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\n\",\"metadata\":{\"output\":\"cd9f132 policies: drop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\n\",\"exit\":0,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"cd /workspace && git add -A && git commit -q -m \\\"policies: drop smallest-change after audit (restates meta prompt)\\\" && git log --oneline -1\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634531679,\"end\":1791634531723}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd64d40019REEwmbc64UE3V\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd5a3a001XREryb9OLeRFxd\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634531767,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd65a8001QZM90gJoc2w5Yu\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd5a3a001XREryb9OLeRFxd\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":39277,\"input\":241,\"output\":75,\"reasoning\":305,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":38656}},\"cost\":0.000380118}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634533252,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd6b800015EDAos5V2FFeoG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791634539449,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"write\",\"callID\":\"call_00_A7VWZbi49JJOo2ajsQzG7660\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"content\":\"# Implementation: policies\\n\\nid: medical\\ndeveloper: developer\\ndate: 2026-10-10\\n\\n<!-- Produced by @developer after implementation. -->\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdded a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog with a\\nsmall set of global, always-on policy files, following the brief's format\\n(plain markdown, one rule per file, filename is the identity, no frontmatter,\\nshort: one-line heading + rule + at most a line or two of why). Four of the\\nfive proposed starter policies shipped; the fifth (`smallest-change`) was\\ndropped by the TASK-6 audit because it merely restated an existing\\nsystem-wide instruction. No code, build, or test tooling exists in this repo,\\nso verification was content review against the brief's decision criteria.\\n\\nFinal set (sorted as the catalog concatenates them):\\n\\n- `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\\n- `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\\n- `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\\n- `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\nTASK-1: Created `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` — never commit, log, print or\\nhardcode secrets/tokens/keys/credentials; read them from env/untracked config.\\nUniversal, always-on, no overlap with an always-on rule in this catalog.\\n\\nTASK-2: Created `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` — leave no debug output,\\ncommented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a tracked issue behind.\\n\\nTASK-3: Created `policies/smallest-change.md` — smallest change that satisfies\\nthe task; no refactoring/tidying of adjacent code, no scope expansion.\\n\\nTASK-4: Created `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` — do not add a\\ndependency without explicit approval; a dependency is a lasting project cost.\\n\\nTASK-5: Created `policies/keep-it-committed.md` — leave no uncommitted work\\nbehind; record changes before finishing.\\n\\nTASK-6: Audited all five files against the brief's four decision criteria and\\nthe catalog content that actually exists in this repo (`prompts/*.md`,\\n`agents/*.md`, `skills/`). Outcome: **dropped `policies/smallest-change.md`**;\\nkept the other four. Rationale per file:\\n\\n- `secrets-hygiene` — KEEP. Existing coverage is role-specific and on-demand:\\n  `agents/security.md` lists hardcoded credentials/tokens as a review\\n  checklist, and `agents/architect.md` mentions secrets management as one\\n  operational concern. No always-on rule existed; a global policy is a real\\n  behavioural change. Universal, short, always/never. Passes.\\n- `no-debug-leftovers` — KEEP. `agents/quality.md:92` carries near-identical\\n  wording (\\\"no dead code, no commented-out code, no debug output, no TODO\\n  comments left without a tracking issue\\\"), but that is an on-demand,\\n  read-only code-quality *review* agent. Promoting it to an always-on rule\\n  that every session sees is added scope, not a restatement. Passes.\\n- `smallest-change` — DROP. `prompts/meta.md` is the system-wide layer that\\n  already reaches every session: \\\"Prefer small, focused, well-understood\\n  changes over broad sweeping ones. When scope is unclear, ask rather than\\n  guess — never silently expand a task.\\\" and \\\"Don't do things you're not asked\\n  to do.\\\" It is also repeated in `agents/developer.md`, `agents/devops.md` and\\n  `agents/sysadmin.md`. There is no way to make this meaningfully broader than\\n  an instruction that is *already* global, so per criterion 3 (restates a core\\n  instruction with no added scope) it was removed. The file was created under\\n  TASK-3 and deleted here, as the brief and tasks explicitly anticipated (\\\"the\\n  final set may be fewer than five\\\").\\n- `ask-before-adding-dependencies` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md:51`\\n  (\\\"Do not install packages without asking first\\\") covers it, and that is\\n  developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` says nothing about dependencies. The\\n  policy makes the constraint hold for every session, which is added scope.\\n  Passes.\\n- `keep-it-committed` — KEEP. Only `agents/developer.md` has the commit /\\n  clean-worktree steps, developer-role-only; `prompts/meta.md` does not cover\\n  committing. As a universal always-on rule it adds scope. Passes.\\n\\nAll four kept files pass the four criteria: universal (every project, language\\nand task), a short always/never constraint (≤ 3 lines of body), no pure\\nrestatement of an always-on skill or prompt, and not situational. No\\nfrontmatter, no id, no README/hidden files/symlinks in `policies/`.\\n\\n## Known issues / follow-ups\\n\\n- The dedupe check in TASK-6 was necessarily limited to the content present in\\n  this repository. The brief references manigot's `internal/session/policies.go`,\\n  its `AGENTS.md`, and \\\"~70 more\\\" skills (`go-code-review`,\\n  `typescript-guidelines`, `security-best-practices`, `test-driven-development`,\\n  …) that do not exist in this checkout. Those referenced skills may later\\n  partly overlap with `secrets-hygiene` or `no-debug-leftovers`; if so, this\\n  set should be re-checked against them.\\n- `keep-it-committed` is phrased to apply session-wide, but read-only agents\\n  (`reviewer`, `quality`, `security`, `tldr`) have nothing to commit; the rule\\n  is a hygiene constraint on final repo state, not an instruction that every\\n  agent must run `git commit`.\\n\",\"filePath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md\"},\"output\":\"Wrote file successfully.\",\"metadata\":{\"diagnostics\":{},\"filepath\":\"/workspace/docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md\",\"exists\":true,\"truncated\":false},\"title\":\"docs/jobs/medical_policies/implementation.md\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634539420,\"end\":1791634539446}},\"id\":\"prt_125bd703d001SN3FiCg5jymgPh\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1791634539501,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd7000001vAK2Iy8wepaccq\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now writing the implementation summary.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634534400,\"end\":1791634539497}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634539577,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd841b001hwAnDlvEP9Xzeg\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd65b40010MtHBEnhhqIGHw\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":40823,\"input\":138,\"output\":1377,\"reasoning\":140,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":39168}},\"cost\":0.001048404}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1791634541120,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bd8a3e001lVhDmwcI8bMpaC\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bd84250012vgwqYi85keHP8\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n+{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1791634542032,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\"