ID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bda71c0019Pb7ReKwxLbt78\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bda153001bEwNOBgXdVGQdT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Done. All tasks implemented and committed on `feature/medical_policies` (branch matches the brief), working tree clean.\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nAdded the new top-level `policies/` catalog directory with short, universal, always-on policy files — plain markdown, no frontmatter, one rule per file.\\n\\n**Final set (4 files):**\\n- `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\\n- `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\\n- `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\\n- `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\\n\\n**TASK-6 audit outcome — dropped `smallest-change`:** every other proposed rule only existed as a role-specific or on-demand instruction (`agents/security.md`, `agents/quality.md`, `agents/developer.md`), so promoting it to a global policy added real scope. `smallest-change` did not: `prompts/meta.md`, the system-wide layer already in every session, states \\\"Prefer small, focused… changes… never silently expand a task\\\" and \\\"Don't do things you're not asked to do.\\\" Per criterion 3, a rule that rules a *already-global* instruction with no added scope was removed. The brief and tasks explicitly anticipated a final set smaller than five.\\n\\n**Commits (one per task, then the summary):** `0c6737e`, `6b6002b`, `26a6159`, `172df01`, `7e415ae`, `cd9f132`, `74d0beb`.\\n\\n**Verification:** no build/test tooling exists in this repo, so verification was content review against the brief's criteria. Confirmed no frontmatter, no README, no hidden files, and no symlinks in `policies/` (the catalog scan's exclusions).\\n\\nOne caveat recorded in `implementation.md`: the dedupe check was limited to the content present in this checkout — manigot's `internal/session/policies.go`, its `AGENTS.md`, and the \\\"~70 more\\\" skills referenced by the brief are not here, so those should be re-checked later for overlap.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1791634548508,\"end\":1791634550129}}}\n+{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1791634550200,\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_125bdada2001uNioLKZIehuuF8\",\"reason\":\"stop\",\"snapshot\":\"\",\"messageID\":\"msg_125bda153001bEwNOBgXdVGQdT\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_eda43d32bffehZumb2jEv7Tiam\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":42821,\"input\":384,\"output\":453,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":41984}},\"cost\":0.000455352}}\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..043e714\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tasks.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+# Tasks: policies\n+\n+id: medical\n+analyst: analyst\n+date: 2026-10-10\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @analyst from brief.md. -->\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+Add a new top-level `policies/` directory to the defaults catalog and author a\n+small set of global policy files (`policies/<name>.md`), one rule per file,\n+plain markdown, no frontmatter. The brief's proposed starter set is the basis;\n+the four decision criteria in the brief (\"skills-vs-policies line\") are the\n+real spec and win over the suggested names/content.\n+\n+Scope boundaries confirmed from the brief:\n+- Do **not** touch `agents/`, `skills/`, `mcp/`, `prompts/`, or anything under\n+  `docs/jobs/` other than this job's own files.\n+- Do **not** add a `README`, hidden files, or symlinks inside `policies/` — the\n+  brief says keep the directory to policy files only (the catalog scan ignores\n+  those, but the brief is explicit).\n+- Every file must be short: a one-line heading + the rule + at most a line or\n+  two of why. If a rule needs more than that, it belongs in a skill, not here.\n+\n+Notes for @developer (not blockers):\n+- The repo contains no build or test tooling; verification is content review\n+  against the brief's criteria, not `go test`/CI.\n+- The brief is explicit that names/content are a starting suggestion. Several\n+  proposed rules (`smallest-change`, `ask-before-adding-dependencies`,\n+  `keep-it-committed`) overlap with existing core agent instructions\n+  (`prompts/meta.md`, `agents/developer.md`). Author them as *universal,\n+  session-wide* constraints (they apply to every agent, not just the\n+  developer), not as a restatement of the developer prompt. If a rule cannot\n+  be made meaningfully broader than an existing prompt/skill, flag it in\n+  `implementation.md` rather than inventing scope.\n+- The brief's `~70 more` skills and manigot's `internal/session/policies.go` /\n+  `AGENTS.md` are not present in this repository, so the dedupe check in\n+  TASK-6 is limited to the files that actually exist here.\n+\n+## Task breakdown\n+\n+### TASK-1 — Author `policies/secrets-hygiene.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file forbidding committing,\n+  logging, printing or hardcoding secrets, tokens, keys or credentials\n+  (read them from env/config instead), written as a short universal\n+  always/never rule per the brief's format.\n+- **Files**: `policies/secrets-hygiene.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file, no code paths or other artifacts\n+  affected.\n+\n+### TASK-2 — Author `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no debug\n+  output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO (without a tracked\n+  issue) be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n+- **Files**: `policies/no-debug-leftovers.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n+\n+### TASK-3 — Author `policies/smallest-change.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring the smallest change\n+  that satisfies the task (no refactoring or tidying of adjacent code, no scope\n+  expansion), framed as a session-wide constraint rather than a developer-only\n+  instruction.\n+- **Files**: `policies/smallest-change.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; the only judgement call is wording to\n+  avoid merely restating `agents/developer.md` (noted above).\n+\n+### TASK-4 — Author `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring explicit approval\n+  before adding a dependency, framed universally for all sessions/agents.\n+- **Files**: `policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file; overlaps slightly with the developer\n+  prompt, so wording must add the session-wide framing.\n+\n+### TASK-5 — Author `policies/keep-it-committed.md`\n+\n+- **Description**: Create the global policy file requiring that no uncommitted\n+  work be left behind, as a short universal rule.\n+- **Files**: `policies/keep-it-committed.md` (new)\n+- **Depends**: none\n+- **Risk**: low — additive markdown file only.\n+\n+### TASK-6 — Audit the new `policies/` set against the brief's criteria\n+\n+- **Description**: Compare all files under `policies/` against the brief's four\n+  decision criteria and the existing catalog content that actually exists here\n+  (`prompts/*.md`, `agents/*.md`, `skills/`); trim wording, or drop a file\n+  entirely, if it is not universal, is longer than a short rule, restates a\n+  skill or a core agent prompt with no added scope, or is situational — and\n+  record any such decision in `implementation.md`.\n+- **Files**: `policies/*.md` (may be edited or, if a file fails the criteria,\n+  removed); `implementation.md` (note the outcome)\n+- **Depends**: TASK-1, TASK-2, TASK-3, TASK-4, TASK-5\n+- **Risk**: medium — this is a judgement-based pass that can change or reduce\n+  the delivered set, so its result should be reviewer-checked against the\n+  brief's criteria.\n+\n+## Notes / open questions\n+\n+- The brief leaves the exact set open (\"names/content are a starting\n+  suggestion\"). These tasks author all five proposed policies and rely on\n+  TASK-6 to enforce the criteria; if a policy fails, the brief's intent is to\n+  drop it, so the final set may be fewer than five. This is treated as in\n+  scope, not a scope expansion.\n+- No human decision was required to produce this breakdown.\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tokens.json b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tokens.json\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..bbbf151\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/tokens.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,12 @@\n+[\n+  {\n+    \"agent\": \"analyst\",\n+    \"attempt\": 1,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-10T12:14:07.370971307Z\",\n+    \"inputTokens\": 27503,\n+    \"outputTokens\": 3045,\n+    \"cacheReadTokens\": 198144,\n+    \"reasoningTokens\": 2733,\n+    \"costUSD\": 0.008186682\n+  }\n+]\n\\ No newline at end of file\ndiff --git a/docs/jobs/medical_policies/verdict.md b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/verdict.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7c92dd5\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/docs/jobs/medical_policies/verdict.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@\n+# Verdict: policies\n+\n+id: medical\n+reviewer:\n+date:\n+\n+<!-- Produced by @reviewer and/or @security after implementation. -->\n+\n+## Review\n+\n+<!-- TASK-1: PASS / FAIL / PARTIAL\n+     notes: ...\n+\n+TASK-2: ...\n+-->\n+\n+## Security\n+\n+<!-- Any security findings from @security, or \"none\" if not run. -->\n+\n+## Overall\n+\n+<!-- APPROVED / REJECTED / NEEDS WORK -->\n+<!-- Summary of what needs to change before this can be approved, if anything. -->\ndiff --git a/policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md b/policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..113f3be\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/ask-before-adding-dependencies.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Ask before adding dependencies\n+\n+Do not add a dependency without explicit approval.\n+A new dependency is a lasting cost to the whole project, so surface the need\n+and let a human decide.\ndiff --git a/policies/keep-it-committed.md b/policies/keep-it-committed.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..3cdb48e\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/keep-it-committed.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Keep it committed\n+\n+Leave no uncommitted work behind.\n+Record changes in the project before finishing so nothing is lost or left in\n+an ambiguous half-finished state.\ndiff --git a/policies/no-debug-leftovers.md b/policies/no-debug-leftovers.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..f992a84\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/no-debug-leftovers.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# No debug leftovers\n+\n+Leave no debug output, commented-out code, dead code, or stray TODO without a\n+tracked issue behind.\n+Remove them before finishing so the change ships only what it needs.\ndiff --git a/policies/secrets-hygiene.md b/policies/secrets-hygiene.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000..7cd6749\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/policies/secrets-hygiene.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Secrets hygiene\n+\n+Never commit, log, print, or hardcode secrets, tokens, keys, or credentials.\n+Read them from the environment or untracked config, and keep them out of\n+source, diffs, command output, and error messages.\n","exit":0,"truncated":true,"outputPath":"/home/claude/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_125bdf409001pS5nBBirBnEdYm"},"title":"git diff main...HEAD","time":{"start":1791634568163,"end":1791634568312}},"id":"prt_125bdf3af001kUyn37z20Z53Ck","sessionID":"ses_eda42451effe3iTssKr1TVXCGU","messageID":"msg_125bdecb4001mrPT0b6sZAv0yR"}}
